@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF4FB
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #355777
skinparam ActorBorderColor #355777
skinparam ArrowColor #355777
hide footbox
autonumber
title Generate Common questions for a requested batch

' Historical filename retained for existing references.
' Request-driven generation: backend/app/services/common_words.py and app/llm/openrouter_common.py.
participant "Common practice service" as S
participant "Question generator" as Generator
participant LLM
database PostgreSQL as DB

S -> Generator : Selected bank entries (normally 10)\nIDs, words, meanings, parts of speech, examples
Generator -> Generator : Build Common review prompt for exactly these word IDs
note over Generator, LLM
  For EACH supplied word, generate one vocabulary review question.
  Return its common_word_id, question text, four distinct choices,
  and exactly one correct_index (0..3).
  The question must test the supplied word and meaning.
  Return structured JSON; do not invent or replace bank words.
end note
Generator -> LLM : Prompt + selected words; structured response schema
LLM --> Generator : Question, 4 choices and answer for every supplied word\nor provider failure
Generator -> Generator : Validate exact ID coverage, no duplicates or extra words\nOne nonblank question and 4 distinct nonblank choices per word\nOne valid correct_index per question; reject incomplete output
alt Provider error or invalid output
  Generator --> S : Retryable failure; do not store partial questions
else Validated output
  Generator --> S : Complete question batch with backend answer keys
  S -> DB : BEGIN; lock and recheck active account\nRe-read learned status of selected words
  alt Account unavailable
    S -> DB : ROLLBACK; discard generated output
  else Some selected words learned concurrently
    S -> DB : ROLLBACK; discard generated output
    S -> S : Rebuild selection from bank and regenerate before returning
  else Selection still unlearned
    S -> DB : INSERT common_practice_questions\nOwned question IDs, bank IDs, prompts, choices, correct_index\nUPSERT progress.last_presented_at; COMMIT
    S --> S : Return questions and four choices; omit correct_index
  end
end
note over S, DB : Generation creates practice questions only.\nIt does not add entries to the shared vocabulary bank, mark words learned,\nor save words to scheduled recall. No Common refill worker or queue.

@enduml
